v0.1.2 — recovery, replacement, and the story runner

The release where money can leave and come back. BIP125 fee bumps land with
replacement reconciliation tested against Core's mempool policy; the export
bundle becomes the missing half of import, with the scan frontier carried so
a restore resumes where the wallet actually stopped; backup gains
resume-on-relaunch with an authenticated phrase reveal.

DNS seeds resolve over DoH with getaddrinfo fallback. BIP352 silent-payment
receive arrives as an explicit opt-in behind a tweak-index setting — scan
crypto against the official vectors, tweak-carrying UTXOs, and the filter
stream pipeline (later moved out of the shipped app entirely).

The resumable public-signet story runner appears: one connected café-to-vault
narrative that drives a real build through every feature and keeps its
evidence. Wallet setup becomes local-first and explicit, and header sync
retries across peers instead of dying on the first slow one.
